(12. AI Semantics) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(12.1 AI interpretation rules) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. AI systems must use canonical concept IDs, not free-text labels, for persistent claims.) Tj
T*
(2. AI prompts must include ontology version when reasoning about capability.) Tj
T*
(3. AI outputs must include evidence references and confidence.) Tj
T*
(4. AI may propose concepts but cannot publish ontology changes.) Tj
T*
(5. AI may infer capability only from allowed evidence types.) Tj
T*
(6. High-impact inferences require policy checks and sometimes human review.) Tj
T*
(7. AI must distinguish present capability, potential, intent, and recommendation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(12.2 Reasoning constraints) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Never infer capability from course enrollment alone.) Tj
T*
(- Never infer verified capability from self-report alone.) Tj
T*
(- Never treat credential verification as broad capability verification unless credential ) Tj
T*
(criteria map to capability evidence.) Tj
T*
(- Never use protected attributes to raise/lower capability confidence.) Tj
T*
(- Never collapse country-specific requirements into global definitions.) Tj
T*
(- Never publish a high-confidence claim without evidence and provenance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(12.3 Hallucination prevention) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Use ontology retrieval by concept ID.) Tj
T*
(- Validate outputs against JSON Schema/SHACL constraints.) Tj
T*
(- Require evidence IDs for every claim.) Tj
T*
(- Reject unknown concept labels unless mapped or proposed as candidate concepts.) Tj
T*
(- Log model, prompt, ontology, and evidence versions.) Tj
ET
